r of the gray square.\n   - From point \\(A\\), she can move right, down, left, or up, each with a probability of \\( \\frac{1}{4} \\).\n\n2. **Determine the Path to Walk Around the Square**:\n   - To walk completely around the gray square, Dora must follow the path: \\(A \\rightarrow \\) right \\( \\rightarrow\\) down \\( \\rightarrow \\) left \\( \\rightarrow \\) up.\n   - This path ensures she returns to her starting point \\(A\\) after four steps.\n\n3. **Calculate the Probability of Each Step**:\n   - The probability of moving right from \\(A\\) is \\( \\frac{1}{4} \\).\n   - The probability of moving down from the point to the right of \\(A\\) is \\( \\frac{1}{4} \\).\n   - The probability of moving left from the point below \\(A\\) is \\( \\frac{1}{4} \\).\n   - The probability of moving up from the point to the left of \\(A\\) is \\( \\frac{1}{4} \\).\n\n4. **Combine the Probabilities**:\n   - Since each step is independent, the total probability of Dora following the specific path is the product of the probabilities of each individual step.\n   - Therefore, the total probability is:\n     \\[\n     \\left( \\frac{1}{4} \\right) \\times \\left( \\frac{1}{4} \\right) \\times \\left( \\frac{1}{4} \\right) \\times \\left( \\frac{1}{4} \\right) = \\left( \\frac{1}{4} \\right)^4 = \\frac{1}{256}\n     \\]\n\n5. **Conclusion**:\n   - The probability that Dora will walk completely around the gray square in her first four steps is \\( \\frac{1}{256} \\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{1}{256}}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{1}{256}}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
